{
	"name": "Frenzyfish",
	"type": "object",
	"img": "icons/creatures/fish/fish-fangtooth-skeletal-green.webp",
	"system": {
		"description": "<p>Schools of carnivorous fish that are found in jungle waterways, frenzyfish are usually docile—despite their name. However, if an injured creature enters the water near a school of these fish, their behavior can change suddenly as they are alerted to the presence of blood. Wounded creatures or individuals who enter the water must succeed a DC 17 Dexterity saving throw to avoid the onrush of fish as they attempt to attack. On a failure, the triggering creature or player takes 3d6 slashing damage as the frenzyfish rip into their wounds, or half as much damage on a success.</p>",
